--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -13,4 +13,16 @@ or when it does not resolve: missing member, array index out of range or not can
 zeros), the `-` token (it names no existing element), or a step into a primitive. Only own members of
 objects are resolved, so `/__proto__` or `/length` never reach inherited properties.
 
+## JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, applies a JSON Patch (an array of
+`add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test` operations) to `document` and returns the result as
+a new value: neither argument is mutated and the result shares no structure with them. Operations apply
+in order and the patch is atomic: it throws an `Error`, with nothing applied, when the patch is invalid
+(not an array, unknown `op`, missing or invalid `path`, `from` or `value`) or when an operation fails
+(unresolved target, bad array index, failed `test`). `test` compares values by deep equality, ignoring
+member order. Two cases the RFC leaves open are errors here: removing the whole document (`remove` with
+the empty path) and moving a value into its own child. `add` and `replace` with the empty path replace
+the whole document.
+
 Run the tests with `npm test`.
